# global-architecture

Shared Blockera package architecture is **not** in this rule. Read it from the global-packages tree (sparse submodule on consumers):

- Standalone GP: `packages/dev-tools/ai/index.md`
- Inside a product: `packages/global-packages/packages/dev-tools/ai/index.md`

After implementation: Unreleased changelog + README only if the public API changed (`…/ai/workflows/changelog-and-readme.md`).

Do not install npm/Composer deps. Run tests with the **active product** scripts (`npm run test:e2e`, `test:js`, `test:unit:php`) — `…/ai/workflows/product-scripts-and-deps.md`.

Keep Gutenberg/WordPress research on `development-helper.mdc` (glob-gated) and command `source-code`. Style pipeline: `…/ai/domains/editor-style-pipeline.md`. Inner blocks / states: `…/ai/domains/inner-blocks-and-block-states.md`. Free vs Pro: `…/ai/domains/free-vs-pro.md`. Task depth: `…/ai/workflows/change-classification.md` / command `classify-change`. GP write root: `…/ai/decisions/001-gp-write-root.md`. Changelog fold: `…/ai/decisions/002-changelog-fold.md`. Product write boundaries: `product-scope.mdc`. PHP hot-path details: `…/ai/workflows/php-performance.md` (the PHP glob rule stays short).
